## 21.5 Python Playwright test

Create `tests/test_agent_config.py`:

```python
from playwright.sync_api import Page, expect

def test_create_agent(page: Page):

    page.goto("http://127.0.0.1:8000")

    expect(
        page.get_by_role(
            "heading",
            name="Configure AI Agent"
        )
    ).to_be_visible()

    page.get_by_label("Agent name").fill(
        "Research Agent"
    )

    page.get_by_label("System prompt").fill(
        "Retrieve relevant documents."
    )

    page.get_by_label("Select model").select_option(
        value="reasoning"
    )

    page.get_by_label("Max tokens").fill(
        "2048"
    )

    page.get_by_role(
        "checkbox",
        name="Include citations"
    ).check()

    page.get_by_role(
        "checkbox",
        name="Enable streaming"
    ).uncheck()

    page.get_by_role(
        "radio",
        name="Parallel"
    ).check()

    page.get_by_label("Enabled tools").select_option([
        "search",
        "calculator"
    ])

    expect(
        page.get_by_label("Select model")
    ).to_have_value("reasoning")

    expect(
        page.get_by_role(
            "checkbox",
            name="Include citations"
        )
    ).to_be_checked()

    page.get_by_test_id(
        "create-agent"
    ).click()

    expect(
        page.get_by_role("status")
    ).to_have_text(
        "Agent Research Agent created"
    )
```

Run:

```bash
pytest tests/test_agent_config.py --headed -v
```

## 21.6 TypeScript Playwright test

Create `tests/agent-config.spec.ts`:

```typescript
import {
    test,
    expect
} from "@playwright/test";

test("Create AI agent", async ({ page }) => {

    await page.goto(
        "http://127.0.0.1:8000"
    );

    await expect(

        page.getByRole("heading", {

            name: "Configure AI Agent"
        })

    ).toBeVisible();

    await page.getByLabel("Agent name")
        .fill("Research Agent");

    await page.getByLabel("System prompt")
        .fill("Retrieve relevant documents.");

    await page.getByLabel("Select model")

        .selectOption({
            value: "reasoning"
        });

    await page.getByLabel("Max tokens")
        .fill("2048");

    await page.getByRole("checkbox", {

        name: "Include citations"

    }).check();

    await page.getByRole("checkbox", {

        name: "Enable streaming"

    }).uncheck();

    await page.getByRole("radio", {

        name: "Parallel"

    }).check();

    await page.getByLabel("Enabled tools")

        .selectOption([
            "search",
            "calculator"
        ]);

    await expect(

        page.getByLabel("Select model")

    ).toHaveValue("reasoning");

    await expect(

        page.getByRole("checkbox", {

            name: "Include citations"
        })

    ).toBeChecked();

    await page.getByTestId(
        "create-agent"
    ).click();

    await expect(

        page.getByRole("status")

    ).toHaveText(
        "Agent Research Agent created"
    );

});
```

Run:

```bash
npx playwright test tests/agent-config.spec.ts --headed
```

## 21.7 Verify the outgoing API payload

An advanced test should verify not only the success message but also that the correct configuration reached the backend.

TypeScript:

```typescript
const requestPromise = page.waitForRequest(

    request =>

        new URL(request.url()).pathname
            === "/api/agents"

        && request.method() === "POST"
);

await page.getByTestId(
    "create-agent"
).click();

const request = await requestPromise;

expect(request.postDataJSON()).toMatchObject({

    name: "Research Agent",

    model: "reasoning",

    max_tokens: 2048,

    citations: true,

    mode: "parallel"
});
```

Python:

```python
with page.expect_request(

    lambda request:

        request.url.endswith("/api/agents")

        and request.method == "POST"

) as request_info:

    page.get_by_test_id(
        "create-agent"
    ).click()

request = request_info.value

payload = request.post_data_json

assert payload["model"] == "reasoning"

assert payload["max_tokens"] == 2048

assert payload["mode"] == "parallel"
```

Notice that the request listener is registered before clicking the button.

If you click first and register the listener afterward, the request may already have occurred.

We will study this race condition in detail in PW-3.
